EIKO EPSON CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOMATSU, HIDEHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, HIROTO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEIKO EPSON CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOMATSU HIDEHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA HIROTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOMATSU, HIDEHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, HIROTO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An ink jet recording ink composition comprising a surface treated pigment which has a dispersing group on the surface thereof and can be dispersed in an aqueous solvent by itself, and which shows an absolute value of zeta-potential of 30 mV or more as measured at 20  DEG C at a pH of 8 to 9 with respect to a water dispersion thereof obtained by 1000 times dilution (based on the weight of the pigment) with an ion exchanged water; and a penetrating agent. The ink composition provides a printed image showing reduced irregular blotting and having high density, can be dried quickly after printing, and has excellent storage stability.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une composition d'encre d'impression par jet d'encre comprenant un pigment à traitement de surface comportant un groupe de dispersion à la surface et pouvant se disperser de façon autonome dans un solvant aqueux, ce pigment possédant une valeur absolue de potentiel zêta supérieure ou égale à 30 mV telle que mesurée à 20  DEG C et avec un pH de 8 ou 9 par rapport à sa dispersion aqueuse obtenue par dilution 1000 fois (sur la base du poids du pigment) dans une eau à échange d'ions ; et un agent de pénétration. La composition d'encre permet d'obtenir une image imprimée présentant une réduction du maculage irrégulier et une densité élevée, capable de sécher rapidement après impression et possédant une excellente stabilité au stockage.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>